      "stdout": "Validate lyra-cli command contracts and acceptance evidence.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  command                     Validate command contracts and declarative Acceptance Cards for\r\n                              lyra-cli.\r\n  media                       Screen media with CCCreator metadata/quality probes and an\r\n                              optional CCCreator/Bach vision provider.\r\n  algorithm-effect            Measure a supported algorithm's observable effect through the\r\n                              configured CCCreator-backed provider.\r\n  draft                       Screen a real lv-draft or offline lv-draft JSON snapshot for\r\n                              structural validity and usable timeline facts.\r\n  trace                       Evaluate an existing command/workflow trace without executing or\r\n                              repairing it.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli lint command --suite registry,schema,docs,acceptance,workflow\r\n  $ lyra-cli lint command --capability draft.video.add --acceptance-level L0\r\n  $ lyra-cli lint command --run --acceptance-level L1\r\n  $ lyra-cli lint media --input ./output.mp4 --expected-kind video\r\n  $ lyra-cli lint algorithm-effect --algorithm draft.algo.ai-matting --baseline ./source.mp4 --candidate ./alpha.mp4 --artifacts ./algorithm-effect-artifacts --output ./algorithm-effect.json\r\n  $ lyra-cli lint draft --ref local://my_project --require-segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli lint draft --input /absolute/path/to/draft_info.json --require-segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli lint draft --ref local://my_project --suite resource,resource-availability --local-resource-root ./draft\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  `lint command` orchestrates acceptance; result lint commands provide report-only evidence.\r\n",
